1 NAME Arvid /Olofsson Drake/
2 GIVN Arvid
2 SURN Olofsson Drake
2 _MARNM Olofsson Drake
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1509
1 OCCU Fogde i Allbo
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Drake_fr%C3%A5n_V%C3%A4stbo#TAB_5
2 CONT
2 CONT =Arvid Olofsson Drake=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Olof Kristiernsson (Västbo-Drake) and Märta Arvidsdotter
2 CONT * Arvid Olofsson Drake,  died about 1535. Joined. Cavalry Captain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Drake_fr%C3%A5n_V%C3%A4stbo Dragon from Västbo, by Adelsvapen]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Arvid Olofsson Drake (son of Olof Drake Tab. 2 ). Died about 1535. Bailiff. Cavalry captain. Married 1: o 1533 to Brita Eriksdotter . Married 2nd with Brita Persdotter (Hård af Segerstad) , daughter of the gunsmith Peder Hård an
2 CONC d Carin Tordsdotter ( Store ).
2 CONT * Married (1)  '''Brita Eriksdotter,'''  in 1533
2 CONT * Married (2) '''Brita Persdotter (Hård af Segerstad),''' daughter of the gunner Peder Hård and Carin Tordsdotter ( Store ).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Brita Eriksdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Märta Arvidsdotter,''' died in 1606, married about 1550 to Field Colonel Knut Håkansson (Hand).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Brita Persdotter (Hard of Segerstad)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Agneta Arvidsdotter,''' married before 1562 with the commander at Gullberg Peder Kijl .
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=17619 Drake af Hagelsrum, släkt, by the Swedish Biographical Dictionary]
2 CONT
2 CONT Drake af Hagelsrum, frälsesläkt, en utgrenirig av ätten Hand (se denna). Field Colonel Knut Håkansson's (Hand) son with Märta Arvidsdotter (of Västbo-Drakarna, see genealogy. Above) the governor Arvid Knut's son Drake (d. Trol. 16
2 CONC 18; see below 1) received 26 Nov. 1574 K. permission to take the mother's name Drake; although he himself usually also carried the Dragon weapon, his relatives kept the ancestral weapon (hand). Of his sons are the governor Knut Dr
2 CONC ake (d. 1639; see below 2) and the governor Hans Drake (d. 1653; see below 3). The son of Knut D. was Major General Erik Drake (d. 1673; see below 4), the son of Hans was again the infamous one! the pirate Gustaf Drake (d. 1684; s
2 CONC ee below 5). Knut D:'s older son and Erik D:'s brother the captain (in a letter from the Riksdag in 1676 called Major) Magnus Drake (b. 1616, d. 1693) served during the Thirty Years' War 1633-37 in the German regiments in Swedish 
2 CONC service, among others. a. under Field Marshal A. Leslie, but must return home for injuries that particularly injured his arms. As a great landlord, he took a prominent position in Ydre, was enterprising and successful, took up new
2 CONC  plantations, built roads, donated to the parish church Sundi and maintained the parish's poor. His sons Captain Hans Leonard Drake (b. 1663, d. 1722) and Lieutenant Carl Magnus Drake (d. 1739; see below 6) became the ancestors of
2 CONC  two still living main lines of the family. Both members lived for a long time mostly as rural lieutenants, and the older line was particularly attached to Ydre härad (Ög.). "In Ydre ... I then had the honor of becoming acquainted
2 CONC  with Bockar, Ulfvar, Räfvar and Drakar, gentlemen of mediocre ambition and thoroughness of mind, as well as among the oldest families", wrote Eric Benzelius in 1732. The older line included HL D's great - grandson's son the music
2 CONC ian Professor Erik Drake (d. 1870; see below 7). The younger line included CM D's great-grandchildren's educator Gustaf Axel Ludvig Drake (d. 1893; see below 8) and Baptist Magnus Adolf Gottlob Drake (d. 1906; see below 9), who we
2 CONC re weddings.
2 CONT
2 CONT The older line D. also included Professor E. D.'s nephew's son, the pharmacist in Hälsingborg, Gustaf Drake (b. 1877, d. 1939), mainly known as a Linnaeus researcher. He has published a large number of writings, mostly of pharmaco
2 CONC logical-medical-historical content about Linnaeus, and thereby performed an important and meritorious work for the medical-historical Linnaeus research. Bl. a. may be mentioned his useless overview «Linnaeus' disputations» (1939).
2 CONC  DG purchased and supplemented a large family archive concerning the family D. af Hagelsrum, which archive according to his wishes was handed over after his death to Uppsala University Library 1940 (27 vols., Sign. X 257 d: l and 
2 CONC follow.) He has in connection for this archive also prepared a typewritten genealogy, «The gamble Dragons» (eg in the National Archives and Uppsala University Library). Some documents from family D:
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://genvagar.nu/show.asp?PersonId=623183
2 CONT * https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drake_fr%C3%A5n_V%C3%A4stbo
2 CONT * http://www.mattiasloman.se/genealogy/5/
2 CONT * http://www.fredrikahlander.com/genealogy/p111ad929.html
2 CONT * http://hem.bredband.net/gunton/6-frls/63_krumme.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Gustaf Elgenstierna , The introduced genealogy of the Swedish nobility. 1925-36 .. Jan Raneke, Swedish * 
2 CONT * Medieval weapon. Jan Almquist SoH 1957: They introduced the common origin of the Drake family.
2 CONT * Dragon from Västbo on the Nobility Wiki. Built on Gustaf Elgenstierna, The introduced Swedish nobility's pedigrees. 1925-36 ..
2 CONT * Jan Raneke, Swedish medieval weapon.
2 CONT * Jan Almquist Introduced the common origin of the Drake family. Related and claimed , 1957.
2 CONT * Disbyt
2 CONT * Elgenstieras Pedigrees
2 CONT * Fredrik Ahlander
2 CONT * ESF Part III p.242b
