1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Märta Arvidsdotter (Västbo-Drake)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Marta Arvidsdotter, lived in 1558. - Married before 1508 with the gunman and the chieftain in Vastbo hd Olof Kristiansson Drake (Vastbo), lived in 1518. The spouses lived on Sundsholmen in the mainland part of Bolmsö parish and 
2 CONC close to Margareta Krumme's widow's seat Sunnaryd (chapter 63).
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Arvid Olofsson Drake (son of Olof Drake Tab. 2 ). Died around 1535. Fogde. Cavalry captain & Brita Eriksdotter.  Arvid Olofsson Drake Married 2: o with Brita Persdotter (Hard of Segerstad) , daughter of the warden Pe
2 CONC der Hård and Carin Tordsdotter ( Store ).
2 CONT *Märta Arvidsdotter, died in 1606. 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000001317841000&photo_id=6000000118088618821&position=0 '''Märta Arvidsdotter (Västbo-Drake) & Knut Håkansson Hand (nr. 59) from  fran Dal - Mörner af Tuna, Volume 
2 CONC 2, page 196''']
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000001317841000&photo_id=6000000089417039889&position=1 '''Geneology Chart for Märta Arvidsdotter (Västbo-Drake) from 63:2 Sparre över stjärna från Jöns Bengtsson t
2 CONC ill ”Drake av Intorp”''']
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT *  Married around 1550 with the foul [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000001317841000&photo_id=6000000118088618821&position=0 '''Knut Håkansson (Hand)'''] son of Håkan Pedersson Hand and Christina Hå
2 CONC kansdotter Tun. Knut Håkansson (son of Håkan Pedersson, Tab. 2, . Death 1565-10-20 (killed in the Battle of Axtorna). Commander (Field Marshal) for all riders banners in Småland and field colonel of the army of occupation in Bleki
2 CONC nge. Became sheriff in 1554 over Östbo, Yästbo and Sunnerbo and 1564-65 held several important command in the war against Denmark. He led in January 1564 a rampage to Halland, fought in July against Daniel Kantzau in Småland and b
2 CONC ecame septtember fältöfverste in Blekinge. Served in 1565 first as "field Marshal" (rytteribefälhafvare ) in Småland and carried out in the summer as fältöfverste a whim in Halland, where he (August 16) burned Falkenberg. Then the
2 CONC  rest of the Swedish army come thither, attended the conquest of Varberg (september 15) and led a division infantry in it for the Swedes unhappy battle Axtorna, where he was killed during the retreat. Married about 1550 with Märta
2 CONC  Arvidsdotter (Drake) , daughter of väpnaren Arvid Olofsson Pull Ke and Brita Persdotter ( Hard of Segerstad ).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Carin Knutsdotter,''' married before 1580 with the rider Peder Månsson Stierna .
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Håkan Knutsson Hand,''' Governor, died in 1633 on Vret, married about 1586 to Virginia Eriksdotter , natural daughter of King Erik XIV and Agda Persdotter.  
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Arvid Knutsson Drake,''' Governor. Took up his mother's name, but kept his fighter weapon. See the plain Meat Noble Meat Drake of Hagelsrum .
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Brita Knutsdotter,''' died 1608, married 1590-09-13 at Stockholm Castle with Nils Andersson Lilliehöök .
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Bengt Knutsson,''' Governor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Lars Knutsson,''' death 1590.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Beata Knutsdotter,''' dead unmarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT *''' Anna Knutsdotter,'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Christina,''' dead 1591-02-16. Married 1584 at Hagelsrum with the castle act at Stockholm Erik Mattsson Körning.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/6656#/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/12580 Knut Håkansson (Hand)]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''By Swedish Biographical Dictionary'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Joined, Chief Justice'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut Håkansson, fell in battle at Axtorna 20 Oct 1565. Parents: Håkan Persson (Hand) and Kerstin Håkansdtr (Tun). Chief whistleblower for a Phoenician Western Gothic nectar 23 Sept 55 — summer 56, joined Sunnerbo 15 Sept 56—10 Dec
2 CONC  58, held various military commands 63—65. 
2 CONT
2 CONT G m Märta Arvidsdtr (Drake), d 1606, dtr to Arvid Drake o Brita Persdtr (Hard of Segerstad).
2 CONT
2 CONT During the Russian war, from January 1556, KH first operated ice in Finland and was then ordered to Viborg. Already in the summer he was released and returned to Sweden. In Sunnerbo he handled the diversity of tasks of a border of
2 CONC ficer, but was soon subjected to suspicion of being involved in intrigues against Gustav I and relaxed. His name under the assurance of allegiance to this 1560 indicates that the relations were again good.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Erik XIV's service, KH made a significant military effort on various fronts during the Nordic Seven-Year War. In November 1563 he was ordered to defend the West Göteborg border with feared Danish attacks with three flags and tw
2 CONC o Phoenicians and to invade Halland where possible, where he plundered in Jan 1564. Still in the spring he was, most recently under Gustav Olofsson (Stenbock), remained in Västergötland but was ordered in the summer to Småland to 
2 CONC assist Charles de Mornay in meeting Daniel Rantzau's attack. He must retire at the end of July for a Danish attack at Tofta bridge. Later in the year he took part in the king's ravaging train to Blekinge and was spent some time wi
2 CONC th a troop force in the landscape, from where, however, in the autumn he must retreat to Kalmar.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the spring of 1565, KH as a field marshal under Field Colonel Nils Persson (Silversmith) defended the small country border against the Danes, but in August Erik's order was made to try to cut off the retreat for Rantzau, which 
2 CONC then fell into Västergötland. As head of a detachment of four flags and seven Phoenicians, he participated in the conquest of Varberg. By destroying the bridge over the Etran, he succeeded in blocking Rantzau's train to the north.
2 CONC  His detachment was joined by the main army shortly before the battle of the Axtorna, where he fell.
2 CONT
2 CONT KH owned land in Västergötland and Småland. He inherited from his mother Attorp in S Säms sn (Älvsb), which he gave his wife in the morning gift. Shortly before his death he received Hagelsrum in Målilla sn (Kalm) in salvation don
2 CONC ation. His genealogical notes are printed in PHT 1901 (cf. JE Almquist in SoH 1958-59). His tombstone in Gällstad church (Älvsb) is of historical interest.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=17619 Drake af Hagelsrum, släkt, by the Swedish Biographical Dictionary]
2 CONT
2 CONT Drake af Hagelsrum, frälsesläkt, en utgrenirig av ätten Hand (se denna). Field Colonel Knut Håkansson's (Hand) son with Märta Arvidsdotter (of Västbo-Drakarna, see genealogy. Above) the governor Arvid Knut's son Drake (d. Trol. 16
2 CONC 18; see below 1) received 26 Nov. 1574 K. permission to take the mother's name Drake; although he himself usually also carried the Dragon weapon, his relatives kept the ancestral weapon (hand). Of his sons are the governor Knut Dr
2 CONC ake (d. 1639; see below 2) and the governor Hans Drake (d. 1653; see below 3). The son of Knut D. was Major General Erik Drake (d. 1673; see below 4), the son of Hans was again the infamous one! the pirate Gustaf Drake (d. 1684; s
2 CONC ee below 5). Knut D:'s older son and Erik D:'s brother the captain (in a letter from the Riksdag in 1676 called Major) Magnus Drake (b. 1616, d. 1693) served during the Thirty Years' War 1633-37 in the German regiments in Swedish 
2 CONC service, among others. a. under Field Marshal A. Leslie, but must return home for injuries that particularly injured his arms. As a great landlord, he took a prominent position in Ydre, was enterprising and successful, took up new
2 CONC  plantations, built roads, donated to the parish church Sundi and maintained the parish's poor. His sons Captain Hans Leonard Drake (b. 1663, d. 1722) and Lieutenant Carl Magnus Drake (d. 1739; see below 6) became the ancestors of
2 CONC  two still living main lines of the family. Both members lived for a long time mostly as rural lieutenants, and the older line was particularly attached to Ydre härad (Ög.). "In Ydre ... I then had the honor of becoming acquainted
2 CONC  with Bockar, Ulfvar, Räfvar and Drakar, gentlemen of mediocre ambition and thoroughness of mind, as well as among the oldest families", wrote Eric Benzelius in 1732. The older line included HL D's great - grandson's son the music
2 CONC ian Professor Erik Drake (d. 1870; see below 7). The younger line included CM D's great-grandchildren's educator Gustaf Axel Ludvig Drake (d. 1893; see below 8) and Baptist Magnus Adolf Gottlob Drake (d. 1906; see below 9), who we
2 CONC re weddings.
2 CONT
2 CONT The older line D. also included Professor E. D.'s nephew's son, the pharmacist in Hälsingborg, Gustaf Drake (b. 1877, d. 1939), mainly known as a Linnaeus researcher. He has published a large number of writings, mostly of pharmaco
2 CONC logical-medical-historical content about Linnaeus, and thereby performed an important and meritorious work for the medical-historical Linnaeus research. Bl. a. may be mentioned his useless overview «Linnaeus' disputations» (1939).
2 CONC  DG purchased and supplemented a large family archive concerning the family D. af Hagelsrum, which archive according to his wishes was handed over after his death to Uppsala University Library 1940 (27 vols., Sign. X 257 d: l and 
2 CONC follow.) He has in connection for this archive also prepared a typewritten genealogy, «The gamble Dragons» (eg in the National Archives and Uppsala University Library). Some documents from family D:
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/6656 Ribbing, Related, by the Swedish Biographical Dictionary]
2 CONT
2 CONT In marriage to Knut Håkanssons (Hand ; bd 18) niece daughter Märta Jönsdotter (Oxehufvud) he became the father of Linnorm R (1569-1627). This is mentioned among Johan III's court people in 1592. Duke Karl used him as the messenger
2 CONC  of letters to Sigismund after his return to Sweden in 1598. R was therefore in the latter's camp during the battle at Lilla Stångebro, where he halted with a fictitious command from Sigismund his noble fan's attack. Several lette
2 CONC rs from Karl testify that at least March was R linked to Sigismund's still barely nine-year-old and already sickly half-brother Duke Johan(vol. 20). From 1603 he is mentioned as his court master, and according to Norrköping Parlia
2 CONC ment's decision 1604, like his brother R1, he was one of the four noblemen who would assist Johan with advice and deed. In 1605, R became his commander in the Eastern Gothic Duchy of Vadstena Castle County, where from 1606 he is m
2 CONC entioned with the title of governor, and in 1608 Johan authorized him to be governor of the entire Duchy. In 1612 he became a lawman in Östergötland, and from the autumn he calls him in his letters (E 5156) advice and governor. Af
2 CONC ter Duke Johan's death in 1618, R again became governor only in Vadstena castle county, but in 1621 his area was expanded to include the whole of Östergötland. In 1623 he became a council, and like his uncle Boo R, he was among th
2 CONC e envoys at the border meeting with the Danes in 1624. R:
2 CONT
