1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In 1548 Patrick Mowat of Buchollie entered into a contract with Malcolm Halcro of that Ilk, in Orkney, for the marriage of their son and daughter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1549 Patrick Mowat sold, under reversion, the lands of Tofts, Overtyre, and Aukingill, in the barony of Freswick, to Alexander Mowat in Tofts; and in 1554 Patrick is mentioned as "Lord of Buchollie and Freswick". 
2 CONT
2 CONT Whether this Patrick was the son of Magnus Mowat of 1522 does not appear. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick Mowat had a son, Patrick, and probably a daughter. 
